{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And the sense of ואקח אותה לי לאשה [\"and I took her for myself as a wife\"].</b> That he took her to be his wife and to lie with her, but HaShem brought plagues upon him so that he would not touch her, and the plagues HaShem sent to guard the wife of His beloved, and the plagues were great, and he could not touch her. Similar is וחשקת בה ולקחת לך לאשה (Deuteronomy 21:11), and afterward it says והבאת אל תוך ביתך וגלחה (ibid. v. 12), ואחר כן תבא אליה ובעלתה (ibid. v. 13)." "And the kamatz of the vav in לָךְ is because the meaning is what is called ענין מוכרת [a recognized idiom]. Similarly לחם וָיָיִן (Genesis 14:18)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:24.054286686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}